[ceiling] Each flat pull roof is the hand-contact face at nominal Z272.194, including the 0.25 mm supported-face allowance. The exterior transition joins this bearing without changing it to a slope. The left mouth opens toward −X and the right toward +X, allowing Tree (auto)/Default supports to exit before pumps are installed. Current full-part support contact, removal and finger-contact finish remain unqualified.
alternatives: Replacing the roof with a ramp changes the lifting contact and reduces finger room. Filling the recess removes the hand pull. Retain the flat lifting surface and its exposed support-removal mouth.
